-- title:
--   Inertia-fixed vector with Frobenius acting as q U_q
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and $g$ a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project, i.e. a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem does not already occur at any proper divisor of $M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q$ prime, $q\mid M$, $q\notin S$) to $\mathbb{C}$, satisfying $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, for all such $\ell$. Let $O''$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a field of characteristic zero which is an $O''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $K$. Write $T=$ [`ModularCurve.TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/ModularCurve_EichlerShimuraData.html#L15), the submodule of sequences $x:\mathbb{N}\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$ inside the $\mathbb{Z}$-Hecke-algebra module $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the Hecke action being `heckeModuleBar M`. Assume given: a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ for which $a\cdot x$ has $n$-th level the multiple of $x_n$ by the representative of $a$ mod $\lambda^n$; a group homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ with $\rho_M(\sigma)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes y$ whenever $y$ is the levelwise image of $x$ under $\sigma$; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from the abstract Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell:\ell \text{ prime}]$ to the same endomorphism ring with $T_M(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$; and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of rank $2$, stable under all base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which the base change of $T_M(X_\ell)$ acts as the scalar $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Then for every prime $q\neq\lambda$ with $q\mid M$ and $q^2\nmid M$, and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, there exists a nonzero $w\in W$ such that the base change of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ sends $w$ to $(q:K)\cdot$ the base change of $T_M(X_q)$ applied to $w$, for every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting as $x\mapsto x^q$ on the residue field of $A$, and such that $w$ is fixed by the base change of $\rho_M(\tau)$ for every $\tau$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$.
--
--   This is the local statement at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level: the two-dimensional $\lambda$-adic eigenspace attached to a newform of level $M$ meets the toric part of the Tate module of $J_0(M)$ at $q$, so it contains a nonzero vector fixed by inertia on which any Frobenius element acts as $q$ times the $q$-th Hecke generator. It feeds the construction of the toric line used in the level-lowering analysis of the Galois representation attached to $g$.
